{"created": "2026-02-03T11:49:36.442417+00:00", "modified": "2026-02-03T23:40:18.925033+00:00", "id": 18467070, "conceptrecid": "15168927", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.18467070", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.15168927", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18467070", "metadata": {"title": "Sherlock: A Dataset for Process-aware Intrusion Detection Research on Power Grid Networks", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.18467070", "publication_date": "2026-02-04", "description": "<p>Sherlock is a dataset developed for research into, among others, process-aware intrusion detection in power grid networks. It is created with the power grid co-simulator Wattson. The dataset was initially presented in the ACM CODASPY'25 paper \"Sherlock: A Dataset for Process-aware Intrusion Detection Research on Power Grid Networks\" and a detailed documentation is available at <a href=\"https://sherlock.wattson.it/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://sherlock.wattson.it/</a>.<br><br>Sherlock contains 3 scenarios, namely 01_Basic, 02_Semiurban, and 03_Rural. All scenarios are of realistically-sized networks, but 01_Basic is smaller and therefore recommended for initial prototyping. 01_Basic and 02_Semiurban contain a train set without attacks, and a test set with attacks. 03_Rural only contains a test set to motivate research into transferability of results into new networks.<br><br>Each scenarios contains:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>network captures of primarily IEC 60870-5-104 from different vantage points</li>\n<li>accurate labels for attacks, recoveries from attacks, benign events, and normal operation</li>\n<li>ground truth data</li>\n<li>device logs</li>\n<li>captures transcibed into the Intrustrial Protocol Abstraction Layer (IPAL) format for easy processing</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Changelog:</p>\n<p>Version v3 - fixed errors in the ipal representations in 01-Basic and 02-Semiurban&nbsp;<br>Version v2 - renamed train.n402.state.gz to test.n402.state.gz in 03-Rural<br>Version v1 - initial dataset</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Wagner, Eric", "affiliation": "Fraunhofer-Institut f\u00fcr Kommunikation, Informationsverarbeitung und Ergonomie FKIE", "orcid": "0000-0003-3211-1015"}, {"name": "Bader, Lennart", "affiliation": "Fraunhofer Institute for Communication, Information Processing and Ergonomics", "orcid": "0000-0001-8549-1344"}, {"name": "Wolsing, Konrad", "affiliation": "Fraunhofer-Institut f\u00fcr Kommunikation, Informationsverarbeitung und Ergonomie FKIE", "orcid": "0000-0002-7571-0555"}, {"name": "Serror, Martin", "affiliation": "Fraunhofer Institute for Communication, Information Processing and Ergonomics", "orcid": "0000-0002-6925-5744"}], "keywords": ["critical infrastructure", "IEC 60870-5-104"], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "meeting": {"title": "15th ACM Conference on Data and Application Security and Privacy", "acronym": "CODASPY", "dates": "4-6 June 2025", "place": "Pittsburgh, PA, USA", "url": "https://www.codaspy.org/2025/"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 2, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "15168927"}}]}}, "title": "Sherlock: A Dataset for Process-aware Intrusion Detection Research on Power Grid Networks", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/18467070", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/18467070", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/18467070?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18467070", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18467070", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.18467070", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/18467070/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15168927", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15168927", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15168927", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15168927", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/rec